  "title": "Rupee rallies to 1-month high amid RBI intervention and inflation concerns",
  "summary": "The Indian rupee gained 0.6% in October, mainly due to RBI measures to curb speculative bets, while the Federal Reserve (Fed) raised concerns about inflation and potential rate hikes. The rupee fell to 96.14 per dollar, but the depreciation was mitigated by foreign inflows.",
  "facts": [
    {
      "statement": "The Reserve Bank of India (RBI) raised its interest rate to 5.25% to curb inflation and support the rupee.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The rupee appreciated 82 paise to 94.96 against the US dollar, supported by RBI measures to reduce dollar demand.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    },
    {
      "statement": "The rupee opened at 95.53, then gained ground to touch 94.96, logging its steepest single-day gain in over six months.",
      "confidence": 0.95
    }
